From d0164206a3c1111f386f9d9c13ed72850400a939 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:45:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: report a rune read on a grid that is already tracked

When the Borg arrives at a Sea of Runes grid and reads the rune, the
function returned false if that grid was already in the glyph tracker,
although the read had been queued. The caller took that as "nothing
done" and went on to its other flows in the same turn, so a step towards
an item was queued after the read. Return true: the read is the action.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#116.
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c
index 5af26cf95..22da02db2 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@ bool borg_flow_glyph(void)
                 /* Stop if we already new about this glyph */
                 if ((track_glyph.x[i] == borg.c.x)
                     && (track_glyph.y[i] == borg.c.y))
-                    return false;
+                    return true;
             }
 
             /* Track the newly discovered glyph */
